   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "סוּלָּם הַמִּצְרִי אֵינוֹ מְמַעֵט וְהַצּוֹרִי מְמַעֵט. הֵיכִי דָּמֵי סוּלָּם הַמִּצְרִי? אָמְרִי דְּבֵי רַבִּי יַנַּאי: כֹּל שֶׁאֵין לוֹ אַרְבָּעָה חֲווֹקִים.",
   "en": "It was taught in a baraita: «An Egyptian ladder,» which is small, «does not diminish» the height of a wall, whereas «a» larger, «Tyrian» ladder effectively «diminishes» its height. The Gemara asks: «What are the circumstances» of an «Egyptian ladder;» i.e., what characterizes it? «The» scholars of the «school of Rabbi Yannai said: Any» ladder «that does not have four rungs.»"
  }
